<title>MEXICO: Amaritel earmarks $600 mln to invest in Mexico.</title>
<headline>Amaritel earmarks $600 mln to invest in Mexico.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amaritel will invest more than $600 million  in local telephone services in 111 cities in Mexico, the company's CEO told Reuters on Friday.</p>
<p>Amaritel is a joint venture between Mexico's Grupo Radio Centro,  Advanced Telecom SA, and  U.S. Global.</p>
<p>&quot;Investment during the first five years of operation will be $600-700 million, of which 90 percent will be to acquire equipment,&quot; Amaritel CEO German Cardona Garduno said in a telephone interview.</p>
<p>- Claudia Villegas, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9549</p>
